WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.708
Should the fund invest in this company?

2
00:00:02.858 --> 00:00:09.619
Use it when: Private equity: a fund buys a company to improve it and sell it in 3 to 7 years.

3
00:00:09.669 --> 00:00:13.789
Ask first: What return does the fund need, over how many years?

4
00:00:13.989 --> 00:00:19.047
Is the market attractive? Size and growth, margins and barriers to entry.

5
00:00:19.097 --> 00:00:25.169
Is the company strong? Position vs competitors, performance and outlook and management team.

6
00:00:25.219 --> 00:00:30.349
How can we add value? Grow revenue, raise margins and buy add-on companies.

7
00:00:30.399 --> 00:00:34.454
Can we exit well? Who would buy it, exit multiple and timing.

8
00:00:34.504 --> 00:00:47.248
Return = equity at exit ÷ equity at entry. A fund that triples its money (a 3× multiple, or MOIC) in 6 years earns about 20% a year.
